fa99e2-1610-525e-add6-ab473d9f6201" :question/math-academy-id "q-177663" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is a square matrix\n- $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-177663/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-177663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-177660/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ab9e2e51-0cf2-556f-b07c-de7c5ce6baf6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-177660/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cb4f7485-bd0e-5845-b5bb-8a7515b95b27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-177660/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #u