ove. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is a square matrix\n- $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-177662/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-177662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84255/selection/44bd3727faa9b8783d947294869df128f9acb5dcb9ad2e859c1fae232710b740" :answer/id #uuid "2ee19a24-d905-5f8e-a846-7eb23a5f1809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84255/selection/92eca8c7cbd6237da4d99b1cd6ebd96ce0a832443c07262b22e0c4a2bdf1921f" :answer/id #uuid "adb09e32-a48a-5f4c-b7fd-b14562314164" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$D$ is not invertible" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84255/selection/11c77ac774fe059c0559f07aaa91c1